<article class="env-lemma" id="05IE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05IE">Lemma <span data-tag="05IE">38.12.6</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be locally of finite presentation. Let $x \in X$ with image $s \in S$. If $f$ is flat at $x$ over $S$, then there exists a commutative diagram of pointed schemes </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ (X, x) \ar[d] &  (X', x') \ar[l]^ g \ar[d] \\  (S, s) &  (S', s') \ar[l] }  \]
</div>
  <p> whose horizontal arrows are elementary étale neighbourhoods such that $X'$, $S'$ are affine and such that $\Gamma (X', \mathcal{O}_{X'})$ is a projective $\Gamma (S', \mathcal{O}_{S'})$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Proposition <a href="/tag/05ID" data-tag="05ID">38.12.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>